{
  "title": "Necrotizing Fasciitis",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/trauma/1007/necrotizing-fasciitis",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jan 1 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Necrotizing Fasciitis is a life-threatening bacterial soft tissue infection that spreads along soft tissue planes rapidly.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis is made clinically with the presence of skin discoloration, bullae, palpable crepitus and calculation of the LRINEC score. Emergent frozen section can help confirm diagnosis in early cases.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is emergent radical debridement of all devitalized tissues with broad-spectrum IV antibiotics.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
